      "description": "Watch Banfield vs Belgrano Cordoba highlights and goals from Argentine Primera División on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 11, 2026. Banfield and Belgrano Cordoba faced off in a highly anticipated Liga Profesional Argentina clash, with both sides seeking to climb the table. The match promised tactical intrigue as these two historic clubs renewed their rivalry on the pitch. A Gritty Opening Exchange On August 11, 2026 , the match began with high physical stakes and a cautious approach from both managers. The first half was defined more by defensive organization and refereeing interventions than by fluid attacking play. Tomas Adoryan received an early yellow card in the 14th minute, setting a combative tone for the afternoon. As the interval approached, the tension escalated, leading to further bookings for Adrian Sporle and Tiziano Perrotta , ensuring that both teams headed into the break with plenty to contemplate after a goalless opening 45 minutes. Belgrano Seizes Control The dynamic of the match shifted dramatically immediately after the restart. In the 48th minute, Lucas Passerini broke the deadlock with a clinical strike, putting Belgrano in the ascendancy. Banfield attempted to respond with tactical changes, including the introduction of Lautaro Gomez , but the visitors remained resolute. The pressure told again in the 61st minute when Lucas Zelarayán orchestrated a brilliant move to set up Lisandro Lopez , who doubled the lead and left the home supporters silenced. As the clock ticked down, Belgrano managed the game with maturity, utilizing their bench to keep energy levels high. Despite late efforts from Banfield and a flurry of substitutions involving players like Neyder no and Federico Anselmo , the comeback never materialized. A late yellow card for Lisandro Pinero in stoppage time served as a final note of frustration for the hosts before the referee blew the final whistle on a decisive away victory."
